# Taster of Wares: X is the number of Goblins Bot1 controls as the ability resolves (CR 608.2c): Bile-Vial Boggart and Taster make
# two, so Bot2 reveals two cards of its choosing (a Mountain and the Lightning Bolt, not the Counterspell). Bot1 chooses the Mountain,
# which Bot2 exiles: no instant or sorcery card was exiled, so a land can't be played from exile. Bot2's own Goblin (a Bile-Vial
# Boggart it cast on turn 2) is no Goblin Bot1 controls, so it adds nothing to X.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Bile-Vial Boggart
Taster of Wares
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Bile-Vial Boggart
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell
Island x25

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Bile-Vial Boggart.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: B)
Bot1.Hand.Bile-Vial Boggart.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Taster of Wares.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Mountain; Lightning Bolt)
! Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot1.Choose(Mountain)
? Exile = Mountain
! Bot1.Exile.Mountain.Play

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 1
Bot2.Hand.Count = 5
Bot2.Revealed = Mountain; Lightning Bolt
